        // of radius r = a/9 rolling without slipping INSIDE a fixed circle of radius
        // R = 10a/9. The decussata has 10-fold rotational symmetry (D10 dihedral).
        // x(t) = a*cos(t) + (a/9)*cos(9t), y(t) = a*sin(t) - (a/9)*sin(9t).
        // At t=0: x = a + a/9 = 10a/9, y = 0 (the rightmost extreme).
        // Has 10 inward-pointing cusps at 360/10 = 36 degree intervals.
